  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be maintained in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation and Block Plan \rExisting (Retrospective) Floor Plans \rExisting (Retrospective) Rear Elevation Plan \rDesign and Access Statement\rHighways Proforma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 3 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen or living room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within 2 months of this permission, details of waste storage and recycling facilities to be provided within the development to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority, in accordance with Building Regulations and Manual for Streets. Such facilities are to be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\t\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices and support borough-wide recycling targets.\r",
    "Within two months of this permission, details of the required cycle parking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThese details should demonstrate:\r\rLocation: Near entrances or main access,\rDesign: Stands\rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit,\rFull enclosed: 4 walls and a roof,\rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions.\r\rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the details stated above prior and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport.\r"
  ],
